{{{{{1<noinclude>|Tip data</noinclude>}}}|Cast-inhibiting crowd control|{{{2|}}}|{{{3|}}}|{{{4|}}}|{{{5|}}}
|type         = Buzzword
|link         = Crowd_control#Disrupting
|image        = Silence icon.png
|description  = A unit that is affected by '''cast-inhibiting crowd control''' is unable to cast abilities, activate items, or use summoner spells. The following crowd control effects disable casting of all spells and abilities as well as interrupt all {{tip|channel|channels}}:
* {{tip|Airborne}}
* {{tip|Forced Action}} ({{tip|Berserk}}, {{tip|Charm}}, {{tip|Flee}}, {{tip|Taunt}})
* {{tip|Silence}} ({{tip|Polymorph}})
* {{tip|Sleep}}
* {{tip|Stasis}}
* {{tip|Stun}} ({{tip|Suspension}})
* {{tip|Suppression}}
|description2 = Note that {{tip|Disrupt}} is not a status effect and solely interrupts channels, and thus cannot fall under this classification. However, abilities that would be interrupted by forms of cast-inhibiting crowd control are also interruptible by {{tip|Disrupt}}.<br><br>{{tip|Root}} and {{tip|Ground}} only disable movement spells and abilities. {{tip|Stasis}} and {{tip|Suppression}} are the only crowd control effects that disable all summoner spells from use; all other cast-inhibiting crowd control only disable movement summoner spells.
}}
